			The LinuxAstro Mailing List

LinuxAstro is a mailing list for people interested in astronomical software
that runs under Linux.  Most of the software packages are ones used by 
professional astronomers and demand a significant effort for porting, 
documenting the port, and updating.  

There are also some people who are interested in porting smaller programs, 
such as utilities for amateur astronomy, and then there are those who are 
working in image display programs for images in FITS format and other standard
astronomical data formats.  Basically, I am just keeping a list of who is 
doing what, and if you want to tackle anything, you can look on that list 
and contact others who are also interested, and maybe save yourself some time.   
Sending mail to "linuxastro@astro.umd.edu" will forward your message to all
people on the list.

All traffic is archived on the anonymous-ftp site "ftp.astro.umd.edu" in 
directory "pub/linuxastro":

File 		Description

README		This file
linuxastro.mail mail that has been sent to linuxastro@astro.umd.edu
maillist	List of people on mailing list, alpha by last name
updates/	Directory containing all of "updates" that I have sent out
misc/		Directory containing miscellaneous hints for specific packages

You might also want to browse the WWW page for Linuxastro at URL
http://www.astro.umd.edu/~colbert/linuxastro.html
Or try the one maintained by Peter Teuben [teuben@astro.umd.edu]) at URL 
http://bima.astro.umd.edu:80/nemo/linuxastro/

This list is maintained by myself (not a list server).  Please send me an 
email if you want to add or remove your name or want to make changes.

