This is to announce the release of svgalib 1.2.9. It has been uploaded to
the incoming dirs of sunsite and tsx and will appear in the appropriate dirs
(see LSM below) and on their mirrors after a (hopefully) short delay.

Since I found the changelog a bit too long let me list just a few highlights
here:

Oak-87 should work again, the 16 color high rez modes have color problems,
 they never worked for any Oak card and noone knows a fix. (*sigh*)

New driver (right now only 256 color SVGA modes) for cards based on the
 ALI2301 chip

Allow to set modetiming ala Xconfig from the config file for all drivers
 using timing.c (S3, Cirrus, Ark). This does not affect drivers that could do
 that before (w/o timing.c)

Support for S3 with Sierra SC15025 ramdac. Some other S3 fixes.

A few ELF/DLL related fixes to Mach32 and Makefiles, 

Note 1: Mach32 could segfault under ELF depending on your setup (gcc version,
 lib, outside temperature..) A common denominator seems to be gcc-2.7.0.
 However, Scott Snyder provided a fix, s.t. this version should cure it. (Mea
 culpa, probably I had to circumvent some kernel misfeature at the time I
 coded that line).

Note 2: A bug in gl_fillscreen under ELF and Cirrus was reported. I'm neither
 able to reproduce nor to fix it. If you are interested find info in the
 BUGS_NOT_FOUND file within the released package.

Note 3: Mach64 is not yet supported. However, I got report that 640x480x256
 works already. Unfortunately it still crashes with the plain VGA modes, thus
 it was not yet included. Mach64 owners hold on, light is near.

Note 4: I'm away during next week (12/9 til 12/15). I should be able to read my
 email (and esp. it shouldn't get lost) but might not be able to follow all
 maillists. In case you want to contact me in that time email me directly and
 give me time to answer and/or get back to my home system and files on it.

Enjoy,
