xpcd 0.3.2
==========


WHAT IS xpcd ?

xpcd is an X11-based Program for handling PhotoCD-images. You can select the
images with your mouse, preview the image in a small window, and load the
image with any of the 5 possible resolutions. You can also mark a part of the
Image and load only the selected part.


WHAT I NEED TO RUN xpcd ?

You need to have X11 running (of cource). You need hpcdtoppm for decoding
the PhotoCD images. And you need an viewer of your choice for displaying
the Images (xv for example).


WHERE I CAN GET xpcd ?

sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/linux/X11/xapps/graphics/viewers/xpcd-0.3.2.tar.gz
(may be it is still in the incoming directory, ftp upload runs this
moment...)


WHAT HAS CHANGED SINCE VERSION 0.2?

Very much. I wrote most of it complete new.
Most important changes:
  - color support
  - the index window is gone, the thumbnail's are displayed directly
    in the main window now.
  - you can switch the PhotoCD without restarting xpcd
  - a lot of fine-tuning.


