Hi, I'am pleased to announce the arrival of NewstoHOWTO in its first
release.  Here is the NEW VERSION of the README file. It was corrected and
I added a very usefull TIP suggested by <smuphy@stardust.bln.sub.org>. So
please replace the one in the package with this one !

- ---------README----------README------8<------8<-------README---------

README file to NewstoHOWTO-1.0   (c) Haykel@cs.tu-berlin.de (Haykel Ben Jemia)

Hi,

the best places where to get the latest versions of the 'indisponsable' HOWTOs
are the newsgroups ( comp.os.linux.answers, comp.os.linux.setup,
comp.os.linux.misc ...). Unfortunately, when you save them with a newsreader
you always have those BIG news- and/or PGP-headers with them (I don't know
if there is a possibility not to have those headers :)).

If you want to always have the newest HOWTOs, you have to save ALL of them
from news. How many ? 30 articles ? And then you have to take all those headers
manually away? And what is about those HOWTOs that come in more than only
one part????? I don't have the time or the patience to do it !!!!

*******************And here comes NewstoHOWTO*****************************

NewstoHOWTO will do EVERYTHING for you. It will LOOK FOR the HOWTOs that
you've saved from news (so if you give him other files in the command line,
it won't process them), it will PUT DIFFERENT PARTS OF ONE HOWTO TOGETHER
(you don't even have to tell him about which ones belong together), it will
GUESS THE NAMES OF THE HOWTOS, it will take ALL the headers away, it will
COMPRESS the outputs IF YOU WANT it to, and it will put the resulting
HOWTOs WHEREEVER YOU WANT THEM TO BE :)

To use the program you only need what every Linux system have:
        * BASH
        * A compressing program (gzip)
        * grep
        * sed

If you don't use 'gzip' or/and you don't want to use '/tmp' as the temporary
directory, change that in the configuration section of the file.

IMPORTANT:
==========
NewstoHOWTO only works for the HOWTOs that are 'posted automatically by the
Linux HOWTO coordinator, Greg Hankins <gregh@sunsite.unc.edu>'.

USAGE:
======
- -> NewstoHOWTO [-h] | [-d] files [directory]
        -h        : print the help and exit
        -d        : make NewstoHOWTO don't compress the outputs
        files     : files to process
        directory : where you want NewstoHOWTO to put the outputs

If there is isn't 'directory' in the command line, the outputs will be put
in the current working directory.
If you put 'directory' in the command line, it MUST EXIST otherwise it will
be processed as a normal file.

MY TIP ON HOW TO USE NewstoHOWTO :
==================================
(This refers to 'tin', it's very similar with other newsreader)

* Start the newsreader ;)
* Go to the newsgroup containing the HOWTOs
* Tag ALL the HOWTOs you want to have
* Save them (in one command)
* Go to the directory where you saved the files (There can be other files in
                                                 that directory)
* Do : NewstoHOWTO * /usr/doc/HOWTO
(change /usr/doc/HOWTO to whatever you want)


If you have any seggestions or bug reports, please send them to
Haykel@cs.tu-berlin.de.


TIP SUGGESTED BY Joerg Mertin <smurphy@stardust.bln.sub.org>
============================================================

Once in a time, at night, run through a cronjob, insert as cronjob:

- -----------------------------------8<------------------------------------------

4 0 * * sun       /etc/rc.d/scripts/NewstoHOWTO /usr/spool/news/comp/os/linux/a
nswers/* /home/ftp/pub/packages/doc/HOWTO

- ----------------------------------->8------------------------------------------

Remember: only 1 Line :) Makes you a complete HOWTO Set in your usual
HOWOT Directory !

So... Have fun !

                                        Haykel

