Version 1.2 of the KBackup backup system for UNIX has been released.


                                 WHAT?

KBackup is a powerful yet user-friendy backup system.

Among the many features included are:
	- support for tapes, floppies and removable hard disks
	- really user-friendly menu-controlled operation
	- afio or tar format =

	- optional compression
	- quick tape archive directory access
	- automatic detection of archive format and option settings
	- double buffering for tapes
	- support for high capacity floppy formats
	- optional public key encryption using pgp(1)
	- automatic handling of multi-volume archives, detects end of tape
	- scheduled operation at a later time or regularly
	- full or incremental backups
	- extensive manual and documentation
	- high portability to other platforms
	- ....many many more

                                 WHERE?

KBackup will soon appear on sunsite.unc.edu, in the /pub/Linux/system/Bac=
kup
directory. The archive file is called KBackup-1.2.tgz . Uploading it ther=
e
proves to be difficult at the moment, so for now, you can already find it=
 at:
ftp.rz.uni-karlsruhe.de  /pub/linux/local/soft


For more details see the KBackup Homepage, including a hypertext version
of the complete manual:

	http://www.uni-karlsruhe.de/~Karsten.Ballueder

                                CHANGES =

                          against version 1.2:

	First of all, ALL REPORTED BUGS HAVE BEEN FIXED. I have also
	detected and removed lots of bugs, that no-one had found yet.

	The new MultiBuf program is now being used to handle multi-volume
	archives reliably and fully automatically. Can even support
	tape changers.

	Added support for "mountable block devices", like removable hard
	disks or just floppy disks. MUCH better than normal floppy support.

	Improved Verify operation. Cleaned up menu structure. Rewrote Manual,
	created FAQ, created KBackup Homepage,....

	many many more...

