-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hello,

I just installed NTFS by Martin von Loewis under linux 1.3.45 and works
like a charm. I used his official release and needed to apply some quick
(and dirty?) patches (at the end of this posting)

What to do:
Find his ntfs sources from:
http://www.informatik.hu-berlin.de/~loewis/ntfs

Download the official release (not extra alphas) untar it and apply the
patches here. Follow CAREFULLY the instructions in INSTALL. The
NTFS loads as a module.

Angelo

===========================================================================
- --- ./Makefile.OLD	Thu Nov 30 13:27:07 1995
+++ ./Makefile	Thu Nov 30 13:25:11 1995
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
- -CFLAGS=	-g 
+CFLAGS=	-O6 -s -m486 -fomit-frame-pointer
+#CFLAGS=	-g -DDEBUG
 #MODFLAGS=	-Wall -D__KERNEL__ -DMODULE -DDEBUG -O2
- -MODFLAGS=	-Wall -D__KERNEL__ -DMODULE -O2
+MODFLAGS=	-Wall -D__KERNEL__ -DMODULE -O6 -m486 -s -fomit-frame-pointer
 COFLAGS= -l
 KVERSION=$(shell uname -r)
 
@@ -19,10 +20,13 @@
 
 ntcat:	dir.o inode.o ntcat.o ntfstools.o dump.o
 
+mem.o: mem.c
+	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -c mem.c
+
 ntfs_fs.o:	ntfs_fs.c
 	$(CC) $(MODFLAGS) -c ntfs_fs.c
 
- -ntfs.o:	ntfs_fs.o inode.o dir.o super.o
+ntfs.o:	ntfs_fs.o inode.o dir.o super.o mem.o
 	$(LD) -r $^ /usr/src/linux/lib/lib.a -o ntfs.o
 
