Pacific HiTech CD-ROM's Linux Monthly CD-ROM (December Issue)

With the hundreds of megabytes of turnover each month on the Linux mirrors,
it is hard for even the biggest of linux hackers to keep up. 

We think we've found a solution by only releasing one CD-ROM, but doing it
every month.  When a new version of GCC or XFree86 comes out you can be sure
it'll appear on the next disk.  We don't have to waste space by trying to
cram everything on every disk--we can be more selective and listen to what
our users want in a montly update. 

In fact, we're interested in distributing any popular Linux files.  Having
trouble downloading that 50-meg file from the net? Interested in seeing linux
for the Alpha or other platform? Let us know, and if there's enough demand
we'll include it on the next disc. 


This Month's Highlights:
   
* CAD, math, etc. stuff 
