I am pleased to announce the first major version of xmtoolbar.

After version 0.63 turned out to be stable enough I think this is the 
time to call this release 1.0. There are some minor changes to 0.63 but 
all in all there are no new features.
 
For those of you who don't know what it is a little description:

xmtoolbar is a simple toolbar for launching applications on a mouse-click like 
the GoodStuff tool (fvwm). 
Some features of xmtoolbar:

	* Group buttons for applications of the same type
	* Quick infos (this little yellow things like in Windows)
	* Confiration is done via a preferences dialog
	* Color Pixmaps
	* Shrink the toolbar by one mouse-click
	
If you want to take a look at it or get the latest version of it, please try 
out my Homepage:

	http://stud1.tuwien.ac.at/~e8930188
 
 
CHANGES:
The pixmaps for the preferences dialog are no longer needed, because they 
have been moved into the code (so the preferences dialog will not be 
messed up when the pixmaps are not in the right place).
 
It is not longer necessary to know the path to an application if it is in 
the search path.

Some other things I don't remeber :-)
 
This version is now available for Linux, OSF/1, Irix and Solaris.
 
I have to thank Renato Ianella (OSF/1), Ulrich Klein (Solaris) and  Andre 
Schroeter (Irix) for their help. 
 
enjoy it,
