LDBF(Light DataBase Filer) - The client/server DBF-compatible DBMS for UNIX-systems.

LDBF (Light DataBase Filer) is client/server DBMS that operates with dbf files.
LDBF is completely compatible with FOXPRO's data and index formats.
Communication between server and clients are made using TCP/IP proctocol.
LDBF uses client/server architecture that means client makes request to
server for some manipulation with database, server performs it and
returns result to client.Client uses standard set of relational operations
for manipulation with database, compatible with xBase-languages commands.When
using LDBF, the requests are processed by server and the result of query is
sent back over network.Such way of processing guarantees consistency of 
databases and more efficient performance.

Features
______________

   - supports DBF database and index files(compatible with CDX Foxpro files)
   - clients access server via TCP/IP.
   - data security provided on server and client levels (passwords)
   - all operations can be stored in log files
   - remote dynamic server configuration  
   - supports transactions (begin,abort,commit) 
   - monitoring server operation 
   - supports dynamic database reindexing 
   - supports triggers,rules and stored procedures 
   - supports memo fields,including BLOBS 
   - supports user defined events  
   - uses S-Lang language by John E. Davis for stored procedures 
   - automatically completes all incomplete transactions at startup
   - includes CGI gateway between LDBF server and World Wide Web 
   - includes DLL of LDBF API for Windows 
   - monitor includes browser that allows insert,delete and modify records

Availability
- ------------
In december 1995 or january 1996 Nadezhda company will issue first
commercial version of LDBF server.Full technical support will be maintained.
Versions for BSD/OS,Interactive Unix,SCO Unix,UnixWare will be available too.
Client's DLL that implements LDBF API for Windows also will be available.

Free version of LDBF can be found on ftp site ftp.kiae.su in 
directory /linux/misc (ldbf-0.9.x.tar.gz)
New upgrades and bug fixed versions you may find in this directory.

Server is available in binary only.

Comments&suggestions are welcome.
Send it to vlad@torn.ktts.kharkov.ua.



