What:
- -----
The sixth meeting of the Washtenaw Linux Users Group.

When:
- -----
Thursday, December 14th at 8:00 pm.
(The *second* Thursday of the month)
(We normally meet on the third Thursday of the month)

Where:
- ------
It will be held at Washtenaw Community College in the Technical &
Industrial Building, room 224 (TI224). Washtenaw Community College
is located at 4800 East Huron River Drive (east of Ann Arbor and
west of Ypsilanti). A campus map is available online at
http://www.washtenaw.cc.mi.us or from the user group home page at
http://lug.nether.net/~linux
Contact Neil McNeight (mcneight@umich.edu) for further directions.

Short Description:
- ------------------
A gathering place for Linux users at the University of Michigan,
Eastern Michigan University, Washtenaw Community College, and the
general public in the Ann Arbor/Ypsilanti area.

There is currently a mailing list for the users group. Send an e-mail
subscription request to Linux.Users.Group-request@umich.edu and any mail
for the group to Linux.Users.Group@umich.edu

Any questions, comments, or suggestions can be mailed to Neil McNeight
(mcneight@umich.edu).

Topic:
- ------
TeX/LaTeX3e installation and use under Linux

Guest Speaker: Gottfried Hogh

A brief description of employing Donald Knuth's mathematically oriented
page markup language for a variety of document preparation tasks, on several
platforms, concentrating on LaTeX3e using a Linux system under X11R6.  Both
installation, startup, and finding an operational "groove" in LaTeX will be
discussed.


