Big hello to all intelligent lifeforms everywhere !

The time of waiting is over !

I just (finally) uploaded the new version of the apcd daemon to the
sunsite.unc.edu. Now, the file is in the directory /pub/Linux/Incoming,
but I think that in the near future, the file will be moved to the
/pub/Linux/System/UPS.

The apcd daemon is the monitoring software for monitoring of APC SmartUPS
power supplies in the "smart" mode.  The daemon is collecting data from
UPS, sending messages about power failures etc.  The new version is able
to log the statistics, handle BATTLOW signal and best of all, there
is the network support for several Linux boxes on one UPS.  The apcd
program is free (as all software should be).

Excuse-me the long development between versions 0.1 and 0.5, but I had
a lof of other work and my free time is very limited.

Best regards

PavelK


